    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my 2018 honda civic is making this really loud squealing noise whenever i'm accelerating. i think it's coming from the engine area. can you explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a bad one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt, or drive belt, is a crucial component that powers various accessories in your engine, like the alternator, power steering pump, and air conditioning compressor. It's essentially a loop of rubber that transfers rotational energy from the engine's crankshaft to these other parts. If this belt is worn, cracked, or loose, it can slip while under the strain of acceleration, and that slipping action is what creates a loud, high-pitched squealing sound. It's a very common culprit for that noise you're hearing!",
      "source": "target",
